# Paths owned by dsf-base, the top of the factory chain:
#
#   dsf-base  ->  dsf-<workflow>  ->  application
#
# A workflow repo (dsf-superpowers, dsf-matt-pocock, ...) uses this file to tell
# which of its changes belong to dsf-base. `scripts/dsf/dsf-sync.sh contribute`
# sends commits that touch only these paths back to dsf-base.
#
# Pattern rules (same in dsf.paths):
#   - A pattern ending in "/" or "-" matches every path that starts with it;
#     any other pattern matches exactly one file.
#   - "!pattern" excludes paths (owned by the lower repo).
#   - "=pattern" names a file that dsf-base ships but each lower repo owns once it
#     exists there (its README, its generated settings). `dsf-sync pull` keeps the
#     lower repo's version of these files.
#   - Later lines win.

.dsf/
!.dsf/settings/workflow.json
!.dsf/settings/app.json
!.dsf/modes.workflow.json
!.dsf/modes.app.json
!.dsf/templates/workflow-app/
=.dsf/CLAUDE.workflow.md
.claude/hooks/
.claude/skills/dsf-
.claude/agents/dsf-
=.claude/settings.json
scripts/dsf/
config/dsf/
docs/dsf/
.github/workflows/dsf-
CLAUDE.md
Makefile
cloneForApplication.sh
base.paths
dsf.paths
=README.md
=.gitignore
